  "transcript_annotation": {
    "text": "Honorable members of the city council, today we face a critical choice regarding our municipal transit infrastructure. Over the past three years, separated bicycle corridors in peer cities have reduced pedestrian injuries by thirty-four percent while accelerating morning business foot traffic by twenty-two percent. By allocating eight million dollars from the urban transit fund, we will construct twelve miles of protected corridors connecting the central business district to the eastern residential wards. Independent financial audits project this will yield six million dollars in annual healthcare savings and congestion relief within twenty-four months. The data is definitive: protected transit lanes preserve lives and fuel local commerce. I urge your immediate approval of ordinance four-twelve.",
